‎
‎## 5. The Invariant — Movement Matters More Than Causality When Stuck
‎
‎**Statement:**
‎
‎> Movement matters more than causality when system is stuck. Who moved first does not solve equation. Movement changes state. Changed state creates new information. New information creates new choices. Choices restore agency.
‎
‎**Chain:**
‎
‎**Links to foundation:**
‎
‎- Choice × Time → Consequence (Dispatch 019) — movement changes consequence timeline
‎- Signal × Time → Pattern — changed state creates new signal
‎- Rule #13: Command gives movement — invariant is capacity to issue command that creates movement, not to argue causality
‎- Adaptability (Dispatch 020): Preserve objective (movement, agency, work continuation) while changing approach (configuration)
‎
‎**Who moved first is irrelevant when both immobile.** What matters is state change.
‎
‎---
‎
‎## 6. Decision — No Gamble
‎
‎> The upgrade was not rejected because payment is inherently objectionable. It was rejected because consistency had not been established.
‎
‎**This is critical nuance.**
‎
‎Not anti-payment stance. Pro-consistency stance.
‎
‎Per [[Dispatch_017]] budget boundary:
‎
‎- Cutting all AI spend isn't option, neither is bankruptcy
‎- Decision not about cheap vs expensive
‎- Decision about: which capability must survive, which spend value can be demonstrated
‎
‎**Tractor fails value demonstration:**
‎
‎- Task = commute (continue active line of work)
‎- Tractor = excess capability purchased to overcome constraint
‎- Does tractor establish predictable, portable workflow? Not yet established.
‎- Therefore: observation, not impulse. No gamble at moment of dependency.
‎
‎**This is Knowledge Quest discipline (Dispatch 018 honesty):**
‎
‎- Observation: free-mode constraint, temptation to upgrade
‎- Interpretation: requirement = commute, not field work; movement > causality
‎- Principle: capability ≠ suitability
‎- Hypothesis NOT YET: whether upgrade would provide consistent workflow — needs evidence (pattern over time)
‎- Decision: observe, not impulse-buy continuity
‎
‎**Time as denominator (Dispatch 019):**
‎
‎- Choice delayed becomes opportunity altered — yes
‎- But impulse choice at dependency peak becomes information lost
‎- Correct balance: move (restore agency) but don't purchase continuity without portability test
‎
