‎
‎## 7. Closing Note — Outside Periphery
‎
‎> Driving a tractor for a commute is outside the periphery. Objective is not to acquire largest machine available. Objective is to move.
‎
‎**Periphery defined:** Actual requirement (commute, continue work, agency)
‎
‎**Outside periphery:** Tractor (excess capability, new dependency, untested consistency)
‎
‎**Final operational definitions:**
‎
‎- **Commute:** Work that needs to continue — actual requirement
‎- **Tractor:** Solution whose capability exceeds requirement and whose suitability not established
‎- **Movement:** Agency restored — state changed, new information, new choices
‎
‎**Evaluation complete.**
